# Comma-separated exact IPs or CIDRs allowed to supply X-Forwarded-For and
# X-Real-IP. Empty means the gateway trusts no forwarding headers — so the client
# address is always the peer, which behind a frontend hop is the frontend's own
# pod, and every rate-limit bucket collapses onto it.
#
# A DEPLOYED gateway therefore refuses to start on an empty value: a cell's
# ingress and frontend reach the gateway from known ranges, and naming them is
# what makes the anonymous and authentication-factor budgets per-client rather
# than per-cell. Empty is correct here and only here, where the peer IS the client.
TRUSTED_PROXY_CIDRS=
